---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Signals from "../components/sections/Signals.astro";
import Retention from "../components/sections/Retention.astro";
import Recovery from "../components/sections/Recovery.astro";
import { APP } from "../data/links.mjs";
---
<Base title="Churn Signals and recovery · OneMRR" description="See which paying customers are drifting away and how much MRR is at stake, then follow up with branded emails and cancellation surveys you control." path="/churn-signals">
  <PageHead title="Churn Signals and recovery" lede="See which paying customers are drifting away and what's at stake, then follow up in your own brand, on your terms.">
    <a class="btn primary" href={APP.signup}>Get started <Icon name="arrow-right" class="arrow" /></a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/docs#churn-signals">Read the setup guide</a>
  </PageHead>

  <Signals variant="full" head={false} />

  <Retention />

  <Recovery />

  <section class="band tight" id="setup" aria-labelledby="setup-h">
    <div class="wrap two">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="setup-h">What you set up</h2>
        <p>Revenue analytics only needs a billing connection. Churn Signals also needs to know when customers use your product, so your server reports a few key events.</p>
        <pre><code>npm install @onemrr/node

onemrr.identify({'{'} accountId: "merchant_123", source: "shopify",
  externalCustomerId: "merchant-123.myshopify.com" {'}'});
onemrr.track({'{'} accountId: "merchant_123", event: "event_published" {'}'});</code></pre>
        <p>OneMRR keeps only the account ID, the event name and its time. No properties, page URLs, IP addresses or user details. Secret keys are refused from browsers.</p>
        <p><a href="/docs#churn-signals">Full setup guide</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What you can measure</h2>
        <p>A fixed number of days after each signal, OneMRR records what happened: the customer cancelled, their activity recovered, they're still subscribed, or the signal was dismissed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>How useful each rule is: how often its signals end in a cancellation or a recovery, and how many were false alarms.</li>
          <li>The outreach funnel: sent, delivered, opened, clicked, replied.</li>
          <li>Emailed versus not emailed, labelled as a correlation, not proof that email caused the result.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .two { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; } }
</style>
